('advanced-native-1123', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1123-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Each score led straight to another comparison, without a clear point when he could stop competing."],"options":["The group had replaced rankings with an ungraded hour before he described the pressure.","He wanted more frequent rankings because the weekly comparisons left gaps he found frustrating.","Each score led straight to another comparison, without a clear point when he could stop competing.","He had entered one short race with an agreed finish and a rest afterwards."]},"advanced-native-1123-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It felt like a never-ending race because he could not find an accepted point to stop competing.","The rankings gave him repeated pressure to keep up rather than a sense that one task was finished.","He wanted a clear boundary around the competition, not simply a higher score.","Finishing one comparison immediately led to another target to beat."],"options":["It felt like a never-ending race because he could not find an accepted point to stop competing.","The rankings gave him repeated pressure to keep up rather than a sense that one task was finished.","He wanted a clear boundary around the competition, not simply a higher score.","Finishing one comparison immediately led to another target to beat."]},"advanced-native-1123-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["For her, the afternoon has become a never-ending race with no chance to stop comparing."],"options":["She chose a race with a finish and a planned rest afterwards.","The account does not show a continuing competition taking over her other activities.","For her, the afternoon has become a never-ending race with no chance to stop comparing."]},"advanced-native-1123-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The future is proved to contain no possible change or rest."],"options":["The person feels continuing pressure to compete or keep up.","The future is proved to contain no possible change