('advanced-native-1132', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1132-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The feedback combined a specific strength and a possible revision without judging the children’s whole ability."],"options":["A confusing draft was treated as evidence that the children could not become writers.","The teacher had rewritten the drafts for the children before asking them to try a change.","The feedback combined a specific strength and a possible revision without judging the children’s whole ability.","The teacher removed every suggestion for change and praised only the children’s talent."]},"advanced-native-1132-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["She wanted feedback to lift children up rather than weigh them down by making the revision feel possible.","Naming a strength helped her discuss a problem without defining the children by that problem.","The comment gave a direction for another draft instead of ending with a judgement of their worth.","The children could see something to keep and a specific next action."],"options":["She wanted feedback to lift children up rather than weigh them down by making the revision feel possible.","Naming a strength helped her discuss a problem without defining the children by that problem.","The comment gave a direction for another draft instead of ending with a judgement of their worth.","The children could see something to keep and a specific next action."]},"advanced-native-1132-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The praise is positive, but the account does not yet show that it helps the children choose a next revision."],"options":["The praise is positive, but the account does not yet show that it helps the children choose a next revision.","The positive words confirm that the children now know which paragraph to revise.","The children have been given a worked example of how to connect the paragraphs."]},"advanced-native-1132-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Treat one mistaken answer as a verdict on the c