('advanced-native-1140', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1140-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["He rejected sacrificing an agreed rule for advantage while still wanting a serious contest."],"options":["Both teams had already agreed to remove the pause before the organiser raised it.","He rejected sacrificing an agreed rule for advantage while still wanting a serious contest.","He wanted to stop all competition because he no longer cared about playing.","He supported cancelling the pause only when it would disadvantage the other side."]},"advanced-native-1140-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Both sides had accepted the pause as part of the rules.","Winning at all costs would sacrifice an agreement just to deny the other team a benefit.","He wanted competition to remain consistent with the terms both teams had agreed.","Taking the match seriously did not require abandoning the agreed pause."],"options":["Both sides had accepted the pause as part of the rules.","Winning at all costs would sacrifice an agreement just to deny the other team a benefit.","He wanted competition to remain consistent with the terms both teams had agreed.","Taking the match seriously did not require abandoning the agreed pause."]},"advanced-native-1140-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["His extra practice proves that he is trying to win at all costs."],"options":["His extra practice proves that he is trying to win at all costs.","He is working seriously while accepting limits on how the contest is played.","The account distinguishes preparation from breaking agreed rules."]},"advanced-native-1140-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["A competitor tries hard but refuses an advantage that would break the agreed rules."],"options":["The desire to win takes priority over a relationship the person harms.","A player accepts unfair damage to others in order to secure victory.","A competitor tries hard but refuses an advantage that would break the agreed rules."]},"advanced-native-1140-v1-b